## Summary

| Concept | What you learned |
|:---|:---|
| **CNOT gate** | Flips target qubit only when control is \|1⟩ |
| **Entanglement** | H + CNOT creates qubits with correlated fates |
| **Bell state \|Φ+⟩** | (\|00⟩ + \|11⟩) / √2 — always agree |
| **All four Bell states** | Φ+, Φ-, Ψ+, Ψ- — the complete entangled basis |
| **Bloch sphere paradox** | Individual entangled qubits look random (mixed state) |
| **Partial trace** | Math tool to examine one qubit of an entangled pair |
| **Multi-basis verification** | Entanglement survives measurement in any basis |
| **No-Cloning** | Quantum states can't be copied — entanglement is consumed |

